      "engineDivergence": "Three engine siblings, and they diverge more than any other family in this cohort. PARTS: modern has 9 (adds header-row and extra); rustic has 7 (no header-row, no extra); classic renders the AntD .ant-collapse tree and stamps no data-part. STATES: modern distinguishes idle/hover/active(pressed)/focus-visible/disabled/expanded; rustic distinguishes expanded and disabled only ([data-part='arrow'][data-expanded], rustic/index.tsx:168); classic exposes :hover and .ant-collapse-item-active only. READS: the three engines read three disjoint naming schemes (see namingSchemeConflict) -- modern reads the {slot}-{variant}-{state} matrix, rustic reads the short palette, classic reads a fourteen-name palette with zero fallbacks, and runtime/bridges/collapse.css reads a fourth bridge scheme that no engine declares.",
